## Completion Checklist

A feature is ready only when all of the following are true:

- The UI and data flow are implemented.
- The authenticated user owns all related records.
- Server-side validation is present.
- Errors and loading states are handled.
- The feature is responsive and accessible.
- The relevant repository tests or manual checks have been run.
- The production build completes successfully.

If a feature is partly implemented, document the missing behavior explicitly instead of presenting it as complete.
